          "id": "3a-r",
          "type": "reading",
          "instruction": "Read and answer.",
          "title": "Airport secrets",
          "text": "Why are airports so tiring? Designers say it's partly deliberate. After security you usually have to walk through a big duty-free shop — the path is curved so you see more products. There are few clocks, so passengers don't worry about time and spend more. And the gate number often appears on the screen only 40 minutes before boarding: until then, you stay near the shops and cafés. Experienced travellers have a tip: check your gate on the airline's app — it's often there earlier.",
          "questions": [
            {
              "kind": "choice",
              "question": "Why is the path in the shop curved?",
              "options": [
