          "instruction": "Read and answer.",
          "title": "Predictions that were wrong",
          "text": "Experts are not always right about the future. In 1943 the head of IBM supposedly said there would be a world market 'for maybe five computers'. In the 1990s a famous economist predicted that the internet would have no more effect on the economy than the fax machine. And in 2007 a mobile phone company boss laughed at the first iPhone: 'Nobody will buy a phone without a keyboard.' So when someone says 'That will never happen', be careful!",
